      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Human review remains because ClawSweeper cannot supply the contributor's real setup proof and no narrow automated repair is currently required.; Cleared: The diff only changes local Web Streams reader cleanup and test coverage; it does not alter dependencies, workflows, permissions, package metadata, secrets handling, or trust boundaries. (sha=6f923aaf07a09acd3d0f88d4ecb87fa444e04084)",
      "review_summary": "The PR adds best-effort `reader.releaseLock()` to the OpenAI-compatible SDK stream classifier cleanup and adds Web Streams reader-lock Vitest coverage.\n\nPR surface: Source +3, Tests +44. Total +47 across 2 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the low-level cause: current main cancels the classifier reader without releasing it, and a Node Web Streams probe shows `releaseLock()` unlocks the reader. I did not establish an end-to-end OpenClaw provider failure from this exact cleanup gap.",
